<ArticleLayout slug="us-ai-disclosure-rules-brands" ctaLabel="Send a brief" faq={faq}>
  <p class="standfirst">No federal law makes a brand label AI in an ad. The duty comes in three layers instead: the FTC's deception rules, a few state statutes with narrow triggers, and each platform's own label.</p>

  <h2>What are the AI disclosure rules for advertising in the US?</h2>

  <p>There is no general US rule. The FTC bars AI content that misleads, including fake people and fake reviews. New York requires a disclosure when an ad shows a synthetic performer, and California follows on January 1, 2027. Meta, TikTok and YouTube add their own labels. hubStudio describes production practice here, not legal advice.</p>

